How it was made (dev-time only; nothing from this is installed in the repo):
  The jsDelivr "+esm" build is not a single file (it imports its five sub-packages from the CDN),
  so the exact npm release was bundled locally instead:
    npm i @supabase/supabase-js@2.117.2 esbuild@0.28.2
    echo "export { createClient } from '@supabase/supabase-js';" > entry.js
    npx esbuild entry.js --bundle --format=esm --platform=browser --minify --legal-comments=none --outfile=supabase-js.esm.js
  To upgrade, repeat with the new version, replace the file, update this record and run the app smoke test.

Import by relative path only (never from a CDN): the app is for children's data, so no third-party script
is loaded at runtime other than the payment provider's Checkout script, which cannot be self-hosted.
